  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The proposed delimitation legislation has triggered significant political maneuvering within the Indian Parliament. Floor leaders from the INDIA bloc are scheduled to meet to determine a unified approach to the bills, with members of the Congress party signaling a firm stance against the proposal. Tensions persist over the potential impact on political representation, particularly in southern states, where concerns regarding population-based changes have been raised. Notable support for the initiative has come from leaders such as Chandrababu Naidu and H D Kumaraswamy, who have also linked the delimitation effort to women's reservation goals. The current debate is further complicated by historical negotiations, including recent discussions between the DMK and the central government. This legislative push follows the 2023 enactment of the 106th constitutional amendment, which focused on reservation for women in legislative bodies, setting a precedent for ongoing parliamentary reforms.",
